---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Pro Service Area Modeling | Mulloy Morrow"
  description="Technical deep-dive: Using unsupervised learning and collaborative filtering to model service professional coverage areas at Porch.com"
>
  <main class="article">
    <div class="article__background">
      <div class="article__blob article__blob--1"></div>
      <div class="article__blob article__blob--2"></div>
      <div class="article__pattern"></div>
    </div>
    
    <article class="container">
      <header class="article__header">
        <nav class="article__nav">
          <a href="/" class="article__back">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7"/>
            </svg>
            <span>Home</span>
          </a>
          <span class="article__nav-divider">/</span>
          <span class="article__breadcrumb">Work</span>
        </nav>
        
        <div class="article__hero-image">
          <img src="/logos/porch-service-areas.png" alt="Service area visualization showing geographic coverage zones" class="hero-image" />
        </div>
        
        <div class="article__meta">
          <span class="article__tag">Technical Deep-Dive</span>
          <time class="article__date" datetime="2015-06-01">Porch Group, 2013-2015</time>
        </div>
        
        <h1 class="article__title">Pro Service Area Modeling</h1>
        <p class="article__subtitle">Using unsupervised learning and collaborative filtering to infer where service professionals are willing to work—powering search and lead matching in a home services marketplace.</p>
      </header>
      
      <div class="article__content">
        <!-- Problem Statement -->
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">The Problem</h2>
          <div class="problem-context">
            <p>Porch.com connects homeowners with local service professionals—electricians, plumbers, roofers, painters, and more. When a homeowner searches for help, the platform needs to rank professionals by relevance, availability, and <strong>proximity</strong>.</p>
            
            <p>But here's the challenge: <strong>professionals rarely define their service areas explicitly</strong>. Some will drive 50 miles for a big job; others stay within a few ZIP codes. The data is sparse, noisy, and constantly changing.</p>
            
            <div class="challenge-cards">
              <div class="challenge-card">
                <div class="challenge-card__icon">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
                    <path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3>Cold Start</h3>
                <p>New professionals have no job history. How do we estimate where they'll work?</p>
              </div>
              <div class="challenge-card">
                <div class="challenge-card__icon">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/>
                    <circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3>Sparse Data</h3>
                <p>Most professionals have only a few completed jobs. Not enough to infer boundaries.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="challenge-card">
                <div class="challenge-card__icon">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/>
                    <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/>
                    <path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/>
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3>Implicit Behavior</h3>
                <p>Service areas aren't stated—they're revealed through patterns of accepted and declined jobs.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Approach -->
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">The Approach</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">We combined multiple unsupervised learning techniques to build a service area scoring system that improves with each completed job.</p>
          
          <div class="approach-grid">
            <!-- Signal 1: CBSA Priors -->
            <div class="approach-card">
              <div class="approach-card__number">1</div>
              <div class="approach-card__content">
                <h3>Geographic Priors from CBSAs</h3>
                <p><strong>Core Based Statistical Areas (CBSAs)</strong> are Census-defined metropolitan and micropolitan regions. They provide natural boundaries for service area estimation.</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Metropolitan areas cluster population centers</li>
                  <li>Professionals typically serve within their CBSA</li>
                  <li>CBSAs capture commuting patterns and economic regions</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="approach-insight">We used CBSA membership as a <strong>prior probability</strong>—professionals are more likely to serve locations within their home CBSA than outside it.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            
            <!-- Signal 2: Job Location History -->
            <div class="approach-card">
              <div class="approach-card__number">2</div>
              <div class="approach-card__content">
                <h3>Learning from Job Locations</h3>
                <p>Historical job locations reveal actual service patterns. We applied <strong>spatial clustering</strong> to discover natural service boundaries.</p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Custom density-based clustering</strong> to identify dense regions of completed jobs</li>
                  <li><strong>K-means</strong> for professionals with multiple service zones</li>
                  <li>Kernel density estimation for smooth probability surfaces</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="approach-insight">Job locations are <strong>positive examples</strong>. We also inferred negative examples from declined leads and "out of area" responses.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            
            <!-- Signal 3: Collaborative Filtering -->
            <div class="approach-card">
              <div class="approach-card__number">3</div>
              <div class="approach-card__content">
                <h3>Collaborative Filtering from Colleagues</h3>
                <p>The key insight: <strong>professionals at the same company often share service area patterns</strong>. A new electrician at "ABC Electric" likely serves the same regions as their colleagues.</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Matrix factorization to learn latent service area embeddings</li>
                  <li>Propagate knowledge from data-rich to data-sparse professionals</li>
                  <li>Company affiliation, specialty, and location as grouping features</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="approach-insight">This solved <strong>cold start</strong>: new professionals inherit service area estimates from similar colleagues.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Technical Methods -->
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">Technical Methods</h2>
          
          <div class="method-section">
            <h3 class="method-title">Unsupervised Clustering for Service Boundaries</h3>
            <p>We experimented with multiple clustering approaches to discover natural service area boundaries from job location data:</p>
            
            <div class="method-comparison">
              <div class="method-item">
                <h4>K-Means Clustering</h4>
                <p>Partitions locations into K clusters. Works well when professionals have distinct, non-overlapping service zones (e.g., "downtown" vs. "suburbs").</p>
                <code class="method-formula">minimize Σ ||x - μ_k||²</code>
                <p class="method-tradeoff"><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> Requires choosing K upfront; assumes spherical clusters.</p>
              </div>
              
              <div class="method-item method-item--highlight">
                <h4>Custom Density-Based Clustering</h4>
                <p>I developed a density-based approach from first principles—later discovering it was conceptually similar to DBSCAN. It identified dense regions of job locations while naturally filtering noise.</p>
                <code class="method-formula">neighborhood density ≥ threshold</code>
                <p class="method-tradeoff"><strong>Lesson:</strong> Sometimes you reinvent the wheel—but you deeply understand the axle.</p>
              </div>
              
              <div class="method-item">
                <h4>Gaussian Mixture Models</h4>
                <p>Probabilistic clustering that models service areas as overlapping Gaussian distributions. Provides soft membership scores.</p>
                <code class="method-formula">P(x) = Σ π_k N(x|μ_k, Σ_k)</code>
                <p class="method-tradeoff"><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> Smooth probabilities are useful for ranking; assumes Gaussian shape.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="method-section">
            <h3 class="method-title">Collaborative Filtering for Cold Start</h3>
            <p>We modeled the professional-location relationship as a sparse matrix and applied matrix factorization to learn latent representations:</p>
            
            <div class="cf-diagram">
              <div class="cf-matrix">
                <div class="cf-matrix__label">Service Area Matrix</div>
                <div class="cf-matrix__grid">
                  <div class="cf-matrix__header"></div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__header">ZIP 1</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__header">ZIP 2</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__header">ZIP 3</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__header">...</div>
                  
                  <div class="cf-matrix__row-label">Pro A</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell cf-matrix__cell--filled">✓</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell cf-matrix__cell--filled">✓</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell"></div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell">?</div>
                  
                  <div class="cf-matrix__row-label">Pro B</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell cf-matrix__cell--filled">✓</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell"></div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell cf-matrix__cell--filled">✓</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell">?</div>
                  
                  <div class="cf-matrix__row-label">Pro C (new)</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell">?</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell">?</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell">?</div>
                  <div class="cf-matrix__cell">?</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              
              <div class="cf-arrow">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              
              <div class="cf-factorization">
                <div class="cf-factor">
                  <div class="cf-factor__label">Professional Embeddings</div>
                  <div class="cf-factor__desc">Latent representation of each professional's service preferences</div>
                </div>
                <div class="cf-multiply">×</div>
                <div class="cf-factor">
                  <div class="cf-factor__label">Location Embeddings</div>
                  <div class="cf-factor__desc">Latent representation of each geographic area</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            
            <p class="cf-explanation">By learning embeddings for both professionals and locations, we can predict service area scores for <strong>any professional-location pair</strong>—even for new professionals with no history. Professionals with similar colleagues, specialties, or home locations will have similar embeddings.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Impact -->
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">Impact</h2>
          <div class="impact-grid">
            <div class="impact-card">
              <div class="impact-card__metric">↑ Search Relevance</div>
              <p>Improved ranking of professionals by geographic fit, reducing out-of-area leads</p>
            </div>
            <div class="impact-card">
              <div class="impact-card__metric">↓ Cold Start Gap</div>
              <p>New professionals received relevant leads immediately via collaborative filtering</p>
            </div>
            <div class="impact-card">
              <div class="impact-card__metric">↑ Lead Acceptance</div>
              <p>Higher acceptance rates by matching homeowners with professionals who actually serve their area</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Further Reading -->
        <section class="further-reading">
          <h2 class="further-reading__title">Go Deeper</h2>
          <p class="further-reading__intro">Explore the foundational techniques used in this project.</p>
          
          <div class="reading-cards">
            <!-- Clustering -->
            <a href="https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/clustering.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="reading-card">
              <div class="reading-card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/>
                  <circle cx="19" cy="5" r="2"/>
                  <circle cx="5" cy="19" r="2"/>
                  <circle cx="5" cy="5" r="2"/>
                  <circle cx="19" cy="19" r="2"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="reading-card__content">
                <span class="reading-card__source">Scikit-learn</span>
                <h3 class="reading-card__title">Clustering Algorithms</h3>
                <p class="reading-card__description">Comprehensive guide to K-Means, DBSCAN, Gaussian Mixtures, and other clustering methods.</p>
                <span class="reading-card__tag">Unsupervised Learning</span>
              </div>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="reading-card__arrow">
                <path d="M7 17l9.2-9.2M17 17V7H7"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
            
            <!-- Matrix Factorization -->
            <a href="https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/recommendation/collaborative/matrix" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="reading-card">
              <div class="reading-card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/>
                  <line x1="3" y1="9" x2="21" y2="9"/>
                  <line x1="3" y1="15" x2="21" y2="15"/>
                  <line x1="9" y1="3" x2="9" y2="21"/>
                  <line x1="15" y1="3" x2="15" y2="21"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="reading-card__content">
                <span class="reading-card__source">Google ML Course</span>
                <h3 class="reading-card__title">Matrix Factorization</h3>
                <p class="reading-card__description">Learn how matrix factorization powers collaborative filtering in recommendation systems.</p>
                <span class="reading-card__tag">Collaborative Filtering</span>
              </div>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="reading-card__arrow">
                <path d="M7 17l9.2-9.2M17 17V7H7"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
            
            <!-- CBSA -->
            <a href="https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/metro-micro/about.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="reading-card">
              <div class="reading-card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z"/>
                  <circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="reading-card__content">
                <span class="reading-card__source">U.S. Census Bureau</span>
                <h3 class="reading-card__title">About CBSAs</h3>
                <p class="reading-card__description">Understanding Core Based Statistical Areas and how they define metropolitan regions.</p>
                <span class="reading-card__tag">Geographic Data</span>
              </div>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="reading-card__arrow">
                <path d="M7 17l9.2-9.2M17 17V7H7"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
            
            <!-- Cold Start Problem -->
            <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_start_(recommender_systems)" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="reading-card">
              <div class="reading-card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M12 2v4M12 18v4M4.93 4.93l2.83 2.83M16.24 16.24l2.83 2.83M2 12h4M18 12h4M4.93 19.07l2.83-2.83M16.24 7.76l2.83-2.83"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="reading-card__content">
                <span class="reading-card__source">Wikipedia</span>
                <h3 class="reading-card__title">The Cold Start Problem</h3>
                <p class="reading-card__description">Overview of cold start challenges in recommender systems and common solutions.</p>
                <span class="reading-card__tag">Recommendations</span>
              </div>
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="reading-card__arrow">
                <path d="M7 17l9.2-9.2M17 17V7H7"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .article {
    min-height: 100vh;
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }
  
  .article__background {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  
  .article__blob {
    position: absolute;
    border-radius: 50%;
    filter: blur(100px);
    opacity: 0.3;
  }
  
  .article__blob--1 {
    width: 600px;
    height: 600px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.15) 0%, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.1) 100%);
    top: -10%;
    right: -15%;
    animation: float-slow 25s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  
  .article__blob--2 {
    width: 500px;
    height: 500px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(69, 123, 157, 0.15) 0%, rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.1) 100%);
    bottom: 10%;
    left: -15%;
    animation: float-slow 30s ease-in-out infinite reverse;
  }
  
  @keyframes float-slow {
    0%, 100% { transform: translate(0, 0) scale(1); }
    33% { transform: translate(30px, -20px) scale(1.05); }
    66% { transform: translate(-20px, 30px) scale(0.95); }
  }
  
  .article__pattern {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 1px 1px, var(--color-border) 1px, transparent 0);
    background-size: 50px 50px;
    opacity: 0.2;
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, black 0%, transparent 70%);
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, black 0%, transparent 70%);
  }
  
  .container {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-6);
  }
  
  .article__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    text-align: center;
  }
  
  .article__hero-image {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  
  .hero-image {
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(69, 183, 209, 0.3), var(--shadow-lg);
    transition: transform var(--transition-base), box-shadow var(--transition-base);
  }
  
  .hero-image:hover {
    transform: scale(1.05);
    box-shadow: 0 0 60px rgba(69, 183, 209, 0.4), var(--shadow-xl);
  }
  
  .article__nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  
  .article__back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    transition: color var(--transition-base);
  }
  
  .article__back:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  
  .article__nav-divider {
    color: var(--color-border);
  }
  
  .article__breadcrumb {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  
  .article__meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  
  .article__tag {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--color-accent-glow);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  
  .article__date {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  
  .article__title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f8fafc 0%, #94a3b8 50%, var(--color-accent) 100%);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
  }
  
  .article__subtitle {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  .article__content {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
  
  .article__content p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  
  .article__content strong {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  
  /* Content Sections */
  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }
  
  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  
  .section-intro {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }
  
  /* Challenge Cards */
  .challenge-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  
  .challenge-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
  }
  
  .challenge-card__icon {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    background: var(--color-accent-glow);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  
  .challenge-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  
  .challenge-card p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  
  /* Approach Cards */
  .approach-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
